/* JukaHub Windows resource script.
 *
 * This is what gives JukaHub.exe its own icon in Explorer, the taskbar,
 * Alt-Tab, the title bar and the Start menu; without it Windows shows the
 * generic application icon for every build.
 *
 * The compiled form (rsrc_windows_amd64.syso) is what the Go linker picks up,
 * so a plain "go build" on windows/amd64 gets the icon with no extra flags.
 * Rebuild it with mkwinres.sh after changing JukaPlayer.png.
 */
1 ICON "JukaHub.ico"
